{
  "id": "area-of-circle-oq-01-oq-02-oq-02-oq-01",
  "name": "Isoperimetric inequality from IBP + Wirtinger + Parseval",
  "status": "completed",
  "knowledge": {
    "insights": [
      "Hurwitz 1901 proof has clean three-layer structure: Analytical -> Algebraic -> Geometric",
      "Wirtinger's inequality reduces to n^2 >= 1 for nonzero integers via Fourier",
      "The arithmetic kernel is purely algebraic - no integrals or measures needed",
      "5 axioms isolate: Fourier decomp, reparametrization, Wirtinger sum, area CS, integral CS",
      "Of the 5 axioms, 3 are proved in existing files (OQ01OQ03 by Aristotle)",
      "The reparametrization axiom is the hardest to eliminate (needs inverse function theorem)",
      "Circle equality C^2 = 4piA is a ring identity; square strict inequality uses pi < 4"
    ],
    "builtItems": [
      "FourierDecomp structure (proofs/Proofs/AreaOfCircleOQ01OQ02OQ02OQ01.lean)",
      "wirtinger_inequality: Wirtinger from Fourier via n^2 >= 1",
      "isoperimetric_arithmetic_kernel: algebraic deduction 4piA <= L^2",
      "cross_product_sq_le: 2D algebraic Cauchy-Schwarz",
      "SmoothClosedCurve structure with circumference and area",
      "circleOfRadius: concrete circle definition",
      "isoperimetricRatio: C^2/(4piA)",
      "circle_isoperimetric_ratio: I(circle) = 1",
      "circle_isoperimetric_equality: C^2 = 4piA for circles",
      "square_isoperimetric_strict: C^2 > 4piA for squares",
      "isoperimetric_inequality: full statement with reparametrization",
      "Gallery entry: src/data/proofs/area-of-circle-oq-01-oq-02-oq-02-oq-01/"
    ],
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETED: Clean formalization of Hurwitz 1901 isoperimetric proof. 5 axioms, 0 sorries, 11 theorems. Wirtinger and arithmetic kernel fully proved.",
    "nextSteps": [
      "Eliminate reparametrization axiom via inverse function theorem",
      "Formalize Green's theorem for smooth closed curves",
      "Prove equality condition: C^2 = 4piA iff circle"
    ]
  },
